/**
 * TASK: Turn an annotated object into an SQL INSERT statement.
 *
 * This is the heart of a tiny object-relational mapper. buildInsert(row) must:
 *
 *   1. Read the class-level @Table annotation with
 *      row.getClass().getAnnotation(Table.class). If it is null, throw
 *      new IllegalArgumentException("no @Table on " + simple class name).
 *   2. Walk the declared fields in order and keep only those carrying @Column.
 *   3. Produce exactly:
 *      INSERT INTO <table> (<col>, <col>) VALUES (<val>, <val>)
 *      with ", " between entries.
 *
 * Value formatting:
 *   a String value  -> wrapped in single quotes, e.g. 'Ada'
 *   a null value    -> the bare word NULL
 *   anything else   -> String.valueOf(value), e.g. 250
 *
 * Example, for new UserRow(1, "Ada", 9):
 *   "INSERT INTO users (user_id, full_name) VALUES (1, 'Ada')"
 * internalVersion has no @Column, so it never appears.
 */
